u  know it's going to be best used to see  to sue each individual person's  immediate needs I mean there may be  things that need doing to the house  alterations that need doing to the house  there may be things like stair lifts  need to be put in you know electric  sockets might have to be altered there  are apart from the hands-on care of  people being made sure everyone's okay  that they're taking their medication  that they haven't had an accident in the  night there is so many different areas  where this is going to be used and at  the moment it is not available you know  families are having to give up their  jobs to look after their loved ones  there also in cases having to sell their  homes I mean I met an 80 year old lady  two weeks ago in Bristol a lovely lady  called Val whose partner is in a care  home and her partner's savings have gone  Belle's savings are dwindling very fast  and she said to me and these are people  that have worked their whole lives paid  into a system and this Val said to me  one options got is I may have to sell my  home and I'm 80 years of age and this  there's no backup plan as I say the  prime minister said he is committed to  fix this problem and I I hope my truly  hope that he will follow this through  and act as urgently as possible lovely  to see pictures of you in the Downing  Street garden with your beautiful  beautiful wife how is she  Barbara you know she puts on a really  brave face especially when we go out she  snaps back into that Barbara Windsor  I know it's expected of me to put on a  little front it's not as easy as it used  to be okay you know for instance on the  way down to Downing Street  I must have explained to her about eight  times where we were going and why we  were going because the nature of  Barbara's condition at the moment is you  know she instantly forgets things now of  an evening she constantly will ask me  when we're going home or where are we or  why are there pictures of us in this  place and of course we sit we're sitting  in our front room people who are caring  for people with Alzheimer's and dementia  will identify with this straightaway for  those of you that can't identify with  this I pray that you never have to go  through it  I pray it never affects you but I'm  afraid to say that one in three people  born today will develop dementia at some  point in time you're going to come  across someone you know whether it be a  friend or a family member that will  develop dementia and that's why it's so  important now and for future generations  that the government acts on this and get  something in place for people that you  know are already struggling to deal with  this illness anyway is hard enough I  promise you and I'm in a very privileged  situation where we don't have to worry  about financial side at this moment but  there are people who really are  struggling financially so to have that  stress on top of what you're living with  must be absolutely unbearable
 

